{
  "id": "SPEC-TSC-CLIENT-001",
  "purpose": "Close defect Families A and B in crates/tsc-client: a session has no terminal state, and the write path is not owned by the session. Today any caller's `Client::request` future writes to `ChildStdin` under a shared mutex (a dropped future leaves a partial frame that wedges every later request: C015/C074; a non-reading child blocks the write past the deadline and queues every other caller behind it: C-stdin-lock-deadline; stdin closes only when every `Client` clone drops: C055/C056), and nothing records that a session ended (a request after the reader exits waits its full deadline and reports Timeout: C006/C013; `shutdown()` aborts the reader before it drains pending: C011/C054; the Supervisor restarts only on `Crashed | Write`, so a reader ended by an oversized or malformed header while the child lives is never restarted: NEW-1). One missing concept covers both: a session that owns its I/O — a writer task that alone holds `ChildStdin` and receives whole frames, the reader task, and a closed-with-reason state set exactly once and observed by `request()`, `shutdown()` and the Supervisor. After this spec, code that writes to stdin outside the writer task cannot compile (the handle is moved into the task), and every listed instance is a failing `cargo nextest` test.",
  "scope": "crates/tsc-client only. `src/client.rs`: `ClientInner` becomes the session owner (writer task, reader task, close-once state, pending map); `Client` stays a cheap clone handle. `src/supervisor.rs`: restart and liveness decided from the session's closed state; `shutdown()` closes the session before reaping and returns the reaped `ExitStatus`. `src/transport/framing.rs`: module doc corrected. `tests/bin/fake_tsc.rs`: scenarios `never_read`, `fatal_frame_then_alive`, `fatal_frame_once_then_echo`, a spawn log, and `shutdown_slow` made to survive stdin EOF. `tests/*.rs`: one test per confirmed instance below, existing tests kept green. Enforcing boundary: `Client::connect` moves `ChildStdin` into the writer task and returns no `JoinHandle`; the only path from a caller to the pipe is a bounded `tokio::sync::mpsc` channel of complete frames.",
  "non_goals": [
    "Wiring the crate into crates/core, the CLI or the NAPI binding (ADR 0006's merge step) — the crate stays standalone and unconsumed.",
    "Typed wrappers over TypeScript checker methods (`initialize`, `getSymbolOfSourceFile`, ...); `Client::request` stays raw method-plus-params.",
    "Family C: header-size cap and rescan cost (C061/C059/C069), stderr drain on non-UTF-8 (C030), header case (C063), execve grandchild (C058), notification channel bound (C008).",
    "Family D: honoring `handshake_timeout` (C-handshake), recovery from the permanent `failed` state (C038), request replay policy after restart (C041), `MalformedFrameReason::InvalidJson` and `saw_header_line` dead code, `SeqCst` strength.",
    "Body-level parse policy (C005, C020, C021): a well-framed but unparsable or mis-shaped body still does not close the session; that decision is separate.",
    "Patching the six listed instances individually (per-call `is_finished` checks, a `stdin` timeout, aborting the reader after draining) — each leaves the shared cause in place.",
    "Enabling `clippy::unwrap_used`/`expect_used` workspace-wide (Invisible invariants) — a separate lint change.",
    "Updating the Lifecycle row in docs/type-checker-integration.md; that row flips when the gate is re-run, not in this spec."
  ],
  "api_surface": [
    {
      "name": "Client::connect (pub(crate))",
      "signature": "pub(crate) fn connect(stdin: ChildStdin, stdout: ChildStdout, max_frame_bytes: usize) -> Client",
      "description": "Spawns the writer task (owns `stdin`; receives complete request bodies over a bounded `mpsc` channel of `WRITE_QUEUE_FRAMES` entries and performs the single `transport::write_frame` per body) and the reader task (owns `stdout` via `FramedRead`). Both tasks call `close(reason)` when they end: the reader with the decoder or I/O error that ended it, or `Crashed { status: None }` on clean EOF; the writer with `Write(err)` on a failed write. No `JoinHandle` is returned; liveness is read from `Client::closed`. `ChildStdin` is moved into the writer task and appears in no struct field, so no other code path can write to the pipe.",
      "error_conditions": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Client::request",
      "signature": "pub async fn request(&self, method: &str, params: serde_json::Value, deadline: Duration) -> Result<TaggedResponse, TscClientError>",
      "description": "Whole request under `deadline`: `tokio::time::timeout(deadline, async { enqueue; await response })`. Order: check `closed` → allocate id → insert pending → re-check `closed` (a close that raced the insert is returned immediately, pending entry removed) → serialize → `mpsc::Sender::send` of the complete body (cancel-safe: a dropped future has either enqueued the whole body or nothing) → await the oneshot. On any error or cancellation the pending entry is removed. A body enqueued before cancellation is still written whole by the writer task; its response goes to a dropped receiver.",
      "error_conditions": [
        "Session already closed (before enqueue, or detected on the post-insert re-check): returns the closed reason immediately, no frame enqueued.",
        "Deadline elapses while waiting to enqueue (channel full because the child stopped reading) or while waiting for the response: `Timeout { method, after: deadline }`; pending entry removed.",
        "Channel closed because the writer task ended: returns the closed reason.",
        "Serialization failure: `Serialize`, pending entry removed.",
        "Session closes while waiting: the reason the session closed with (`Crashed`, `Write`, `Read`, `MalformedFrame`, `OversizedFrame`, or `SessionClosed` after `shutdown`)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Client::closed",
      "signature": "pub fn closed(&self) -> Option<TscClientError>",
      "description": "`Some(reason)` once the session has ended, `None` while live. Set exactly once, by the first of: reader exit, writer write failure, `Supervisor::shutdown`. Every later `closed()` call returns a clone of the same reason. Closing fails every pending waiter with the reason and signals the writer task to drop `ChildStdin` (the pipe closes even while `Client` clones are alive).",
      "error_conditions": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Supervisor::request",
      "signature": "pub async fn request(&mut self, method: &str, params: serde_json::Value, deadline: Duration) -> Result<TaggedResponse, TscClientError>",
      "description": "Restart rule: if `self.client.closed()` is `Some` before the call, restart first (budget permitting), then send once. If the call fails and `self.client.closed()` is now `Some`, restart once and retry once. The decision reads the closed state only — `supervisor.rs` matches no `TscClientError` variant and polls no `JoinHandle`. A closed session of any reason is a session-ended state.",
      "error_conditions": [
        "`failed` set or restart budget exhausted: `RestartStormDetected { attempts, window }`, unchanged.",
        "Restart spawn failure: the spawn error (`SpawnFailed`, `UnsupportedVersion`, `VersionCheckFailed`).",
        "Retry after restart fails: that error, unchanged (a `Timeout` on a live session is not a restart trigger)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Supervisor::is_alive",
      "signature": "pub fn is_alive(&self) -> bool",
      "description": "`self.client.closed().is_none() && !self.failed`. The `reader_handle` field and `JoinHandle::is_finished` are removed; the closed state is the single liveness source.",
      "error_conditions": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Supervisor::shutdown",
      "signature": "pub async fn shutdown(self) -> Result<std::process::ExitStatus, TscClientError>",
      "description": "Order: `close(SessionClosed)` (fails all pending, writer drops stdin so the child sees EOF regardless of clones) → race `SHUTDOWN_GRACE` against `child.wait()` → past it, `start_kill` then unconditional `wait()`. Returns the reaped status instead of discarding it (C-crashed-status). The reader task is not aborted before close; it exits on stdout EOF.",
      "error_conditions": [
        "`child.wait()` I/O failure inside the grace window: `Reap(err)`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Supervisor::client (doc)",
      "signature": "pub fn client(&self) -> Client",
      "description": "Doc says: a clone obtained before a restart fails immediately with the reason that session closed with (`Crashed`, `Write`, `Read`, `MalformedFrame`, `OversizedFrame`); a clone held across `shutdown` fails with `SessionClosed`. The current promise of `SessionClosed` for stale clones is removed.",
      "error_conditions": []
    },
    {
      "name": "fake-tsc scenarios",
      "signature": "FAKE_TSC_SCENARIO = never_read | fatal_frame_then_alive | fatal_frame_once_then_echo | shutdown_slow:<ms> (changed)",
      "description": "`never_read`: never reads stdin, never writes stdout, sleeps until killed. `fatal_frame_then_alive`: writes the headerless block from `garbage_bytes`, then reads and discards stdin forever without exiting. `fatal_frame_once_then_echo`: on the first spawn in this `cwd` behaves as `fatal_frame_then_alive`; on every later spawn behaves as `echo`. `shutdown_slow:<ms>` (changed): keeps sleeping after stdin EOF instead of breaking, so the supervisor's force-kill branch is reached. Every scenario appends one line (its PID) to `<cwd>/fake-tsc-spawns.log` at startup; `fatal_frame_once_then_echo` reads that file's line count before appending to decide which spawn it is, and tests read it to assert spawn counts.",
      "error_conditions": []
    }
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC-1",
      "criterion": "Compile-time ownership: after this change `grep -rn 'ChildStdin' crates/tsc-client/src` matches only `spawn_process`'s `child.stdin.take()` site and `Client::connect`'s parameter plus the writer task's `move` closure; no struct declares a field of type `ChildStdin` or `AsyncMutex<ChildStdin>`; `transport::write_frame(` is called from exactly one site under `crates/tsc-client/src/` (the writer task). `framing.rs`'s module doc no longer contains the sentence beginning \"Writing has no equivalent partial-state problem\" and instead states that only the writer task writes, one whole frame per channel message. Verified by the greps above run in review and by `cargo clippy -p oxc-react-docgen-tsc-client -- -D warnings` passing.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-2",
      "criterion": "C015/C074 — `tests/lifecycle_cancelled_request.rs::dropping_a_request_future_mid_write_never_wedges_the_session`: with the `echo` fake, build `client.request(\"big\", json!({\"blob\": \"x\".repeat(8 * 1024 * 1024)}), 10s)`, wrap it in `tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_millis(1), ..)`, await (it elapses) and drop it; then `client.request(\"ping\", json!({}), 2s)` on the same `Client` returns `Ok` with `value[\"echo\"]` equal to `json!({})` and `is_alive()` is true. Today this test fails with `Timeout` on the ping.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-3",
      "criterion": "C-stdin-lock-deadline — `tests/lifecycle_timeout.rs::a_child_that_stops_reading_stdin_cannot_hold_a_request_past_its_deadline`: with the `never_read` fake, issue 8 concurrent `client.request(\"big\", json!({\"blob\": \"x\".repeat(1024 * 1024)}), 100ms)` via `tokio::join!`; every result is `Err(Timeout { after: 100ms, .. })` and every request's own elapsed time is under 500 ms (measured with `Instant` around each future). Then `supervisor.shutdown().await` returns `Ok(_)` within 5 s (writer drops stdin from inside a blocked write; grace then SIGKILL). Today the first request blocks 2 s or more.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-4",
      "criterion": "C055/C056 — `tests/lifecycle_shutdown_reaping.rs::shutdown_closes_stdin_while_a_client_clone_is_held`: with the `echo` fake, hold `let _clone = supervisor.client();` across `supervisor.shutdown().await`; it returns `Ok(status)` with `status.success()` and elapsed under 1 s (the child exits on stdin EOF; the 2 s grace window is not consumed). Today elapsed is 2.0 s.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-5",
      "criterion": "Force-kill branch reached — `shutdown_force_kills_and_reaps_a_process_that_ignores_it` uses the changed `shutdown_slow:30000` (survives stdin EOF) and asserts `Ok(status)` with `!status.success()`, elapsed at least 2 s (`SHUTDOWN_GRACE`) and under 10 s. Today the fake exits at stdin EOF in ~107 ms and the branch is never exercised.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-6",
      "criterion": "C006/C013 — `tests/lifecycle_malformed_or_oversized_frame.rs::a_request_after_the_reader_ended_fails_immediately_with_the_closed_reason`: with the `garbage_bytes` fake and the raw `Client` from `supervisor.client()`, the first `request(\"ping\", json!({}), 2s)` returns `Err(MalformedFrame { reason: NoContentLengthHeader })`; a second `request(\"ping\", json!({}), 3s)` returns the same error in under 100 ms; `client.closed()` is `Some(MalformedFrame { reason: NoContentLengthHeader })` on two consecutive calls. Today the second request returns `Timeout` after 3.0 s.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-7",
      "criterion": "C011/C054 — `tests/lifecycle_shutdown_reaping.rs::shutdown_fails_in_flight_requests_on_clones_with_session_closed`: with the `never_respond` fake, `let client = supervisor.client(); let in_flight = tokio::spawn(async move { client.request(\"ping\", json!({}), 30s).await });` after a 50 ms sleep call `supervisor.shutdown().await` (returns `Ok`); `in_flight.await` yields `Err(SessionClosed)` within 1 s of shutdown starting. Today it yields `Timeout` after 30 s.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-8",
      "criterion": "SessionClosed reachability — same file, `a_clone_held_across_shutdown_reports_session_closed`: `let stale = supervisor.client(); supervisor.shutdown().await.unwrap();` then `stale.closed()` is `Some(SessionClosed)` and `stale.request(\"ping\", json!({}), 2s)` returns `Err(SessionClosed)` in under 100 ms.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-9",
      "criterion": "NEW-1 recovery — `tests/lifecycle_crash.rs::a_fatal_frame_from_a_live_child_is_restarted_not_timed_out`: with the `fatal_frame_once_then_echo` fake, `supervisor.request(\"ping\", json!({\"n\": 1}), 2s)` returns `Ok` with `value[\"echo\"]` equal to `json!({\"n\": 1})`; afterwards `is_alive()` is true, `<cwd>/fake-tsc-spawns.log` has exactly 2 lines, and a second `supervisor.request` returns `Ok` with the log still at 2 lines. Today the first call returns `Timeout`, the log has 1 line and `is_alive()` is false.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-10",
      "criterion": "NEW-1 storm accounting — same file, `a_child_that_always_sends_a_fatal_frame_consumes_the_restart_budget`: with the `fatal_frame_then_alive` fake, three consecutive `supervisor.request(\"ping\", json!({}), 300ms)` calls each return `Err(MalformedFrame { .. })` (never `Timeout`), the fourth returns `Err(RestartStormDetected { attempts: 3, .. })`, and `fake-tsc-spawns.log` has exactly 4 lines (initial spawn plus three restarts). Today all four calls return `Timeout` and the log has 1 line.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-11",
      "criterion": "Restart decided from state, not variants — `grep -n 'is_finished\\|Crashed { .. } | TscClientError::Write\\|reader_handle' crates/tsc-client/src/supervisor.rs` matches nothing; `Supervisor` has no `JoinHandle` field. Behaviorally covered by AC-9 and AC-10 (a `MalformedFrame` closure restarts) together with the existing `a_request_the_child_never_answers_times_out` (a `Timeout` on a live session does not restart: after it, `fake-tsc-spawns.log` has exactly 1 line — add this assertion).",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-12",
      "criterion": "Stale clone after restart — `tests/lifecycle_crash.rs::a_clone_from_before_a_restart_fails_immediately_with_the_old_sessions_reason`: with `exit_after:1:7`, `let stale = supervisor.client();` then `supervisor.request` twice (the second call restarts and returns `Ok`); `stale.request(\"ping\", json!({}), 2s)` returns `Err(Crashed { .. })` or `Err(Write(_))` in under 100 ms and `stale.closed()` is `Some` of the same variant; `supervisor.client().request(\"ping\", json!({}), 2s)` returns `Ok`.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-13",
      "criterion": "C-crashed-status — `tests/lifecycle_shutdown_reaping.rs::shutdown_returns_the_reaped_exit_status`: with `exit_after:1:7`, one `supervisor.request` returns `Ok`; after a 100 ms sleep `supervisor.shutdown().await` returns `Ok(status)` with `status.code() == Some(7)`. Today `shutdown` returns `Ok(())` and the status is dropped.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-14",
      "criterion": "Close is set once — `tests/lifecycle_crash.rs::the_first_close_reason_wins`: with `exit_after:1:7`, issue `request(\"a\")` and `request(\"b\")` concurrently on the raw `Client` with 2 s deadlines; exactly one is `Ok`, the other is `Err(Crashed { .. })` or `Err(Write(_))` (not `Timeout`), both complete in under 1 s, and `client.closed()` called three times returns the same variant each time.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-15",
      "criterion": "Existing suite stays green with the new restart rule: `cargo nextest run -p oxc-react-docgen-tsc-client --locked` and `cargo test --doc -p oxc-react-docgen-tsc-client` pass; the four `expect_malformed`/oversized tests still observe their `MalformedFrame`/`OversizedFrame` variant (now after one restart-and-retry against a fresh fake that misbehaves again) and each completes in under 2 s; `cargo clippy -p oxc-react-docgen-tsc-client --locked -- -D warnings` and `cargo fmt --check` pass. These run in CI via `just lint` and `just test-rust`.",
      "is_error_case": false
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": "Shape chosen: the caller's proposed shape, with two narrowings. (1) No new `Session` type is required; `ClientInner` already is the per-session shared state and gains the writer sender and closed state — a rename is optional and not a criterion. (2) `shutdown` fails pending immediately with `SessionClosed` rather than draining responses: it is deterministic, matches the doc's existing promise, and the real tsc exits on stdin EOF in about 1 ms, so a grace window buys nothing today. Decisions the user must make (each has a default already written into the criteria; a different answer changes the named criterion): Q1 write-queue capacity — bounded `mpsc` of 16 whole frames as a `const WRITE_QUEUE_FRAMES`; make it a `SupervisorConfig` field instead? An unbounded channel would make enqueue instant but let memory grow without bound against a non-reading child. Q2 shutdown grace for in-flight requests — fail-fast `SessionClosed` (default) or let responses land for up to `SHUTDOWN_GRACE` before closing stdin? Q3 `shutdown` returning `ExitStatus` — public signature change on an unconsumed crate; the alternative is to keep `Ok(())` and drop the always-`None` `Crashed.status` field. Q4 restart on every closed reason — a child that always emits a bad header now burns the 3-restart budget in 3 calls (AC-10); confirm that accounting is wanted rather than treating `MalformedFrame`/`OversizedFrame` as non-restartable. Q5 stale-clone error — the old session's true reason (default) versus remapping to `SessionClosed` at restart (would require the supervisor to override a set-once state). Family C/D items touched only where the change covers them: C-crashed-status (AC-13), SessionClosed reachability (AC-8), the force-kill test gap (AC-5). No persisted arch model exists at docs/architecture/model.json and docs/architecture/README.md does not cover crates/tsc-client — coverage gap; audit-architecture should bootstrap it after implementation with the invariant 'only the writer task holds ChildStdin; a session closes once, with a reason'. ADR: yes — one short record (0007). Gate 1: it sets a boundary (single writer task, close-once state) that the later typed-checker layer, handshake work and core wiring must respect. Gate 2: a reader seeing a channel and a task where a mutex would do will plausibly revert to the mutex; framing.rs's module doc already asserted the false 'no partial-state problem' invariant. Enforced by AC-2/AC-3/AC-7 tests."
}

